# SherehePass environment.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development. On a host, set these as environment
# variables instead — there is no .env in a deployment.
#
# `scripts/check-env.mjs` runs first in `npm run build` and refuses a deploy
# build with any of these wrong. Locally the same problems are printed as
# notes, so a local build never blocks.

# --- Database -----------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres. Local development uses the workspace Docker instance on 5433
# (not 5432 — something native on this machine holds that port).
#
#   postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/sherehepass?schema=public
#
# This is needed BY THE BUILD, not only at runtime: app/sitemap.ts queries the
# database and Next prerenders it. So the deploy order is migrate, then build.
# A managed Postgres that only accepts pooled connections still works, but the
# migration must run against the direct (unpooled) URL.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname?schema=public"

# --- Auth ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs every session cookie. Generate one with:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Never reuse the value from another environment, and never the placeholder
# below: anyone who can read it can mint an admin session. The build refuses a
# secret shorter than 32 characters or one that still looks like a placeholder.
JWT_SECRET="generate-with-openssl-rand-hex-32"

# --- Public URL ---------------------------------------------------------
# The site's own origin, no trailing slash. Inlined at build time and used for
# every canonical, Open Graph URL and sitemap entry, so it has to be the real
# https origin at the moment the build runs — not a value patched in later.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3002"

# --- Payments (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# Payments are simulated. No money moves and no card or M-Pesa credentials are
# ever collected.
#
# How often a simulated payment fails, so the release path (putting unpaid
# tickets back on sale) actually gets exercised. Default 0.125, one in eight.
# Set to 0 for a deterministic scripted run.
# PAYMENT_FAILURE_RATE="0.125"
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY and MPESA_CONSUMER_KEY are read by `gatewayMode()` in
# lib/payments.ts, but no live gateway is implemented. Setting either one does
# not enable real payments — it only stops the simulated callback being
# scheduled, leaving every order unpaid and no ticket ever minted. The build
# refuses them for that reason. Leave both unset.
